  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.25.1 release assets and hashed independently. v5.25.1 routes every download in install.sh through one seam, which is what makes it able to tell a transient failure from a permanent one: an HTTP 5xx, a 429 or a curl transport error says it is transient and says to retry later, and a 404 deliberately does not. It does not retry on its own -- a silent retry hides that the problem is on the other side. The nvm download was the only one of the five without -f, so curl exited 0 on an HTTP error and piped the error body into bash; a 503 from the Buenos Aires CDN edge reached bash as a script and killed a clean-account install with two syntax errors. Downloaded installers are now saved and run from a file instead of piped, and their temp directory is removed by a trap. Separately, the five version probes gained || true: under set -e an assignment whose command substitution exits non-zero aborted the whole script with no output at all. Unlike the previous two releases, install.sh is NOT byte-identical to v5.23.0 -- it is the file this release changed, so DARQ's own installer changes with it. build_zipapp.py and build_installer.py stay byte-identical."
  }
